Model interpretation and development of new stage system
The time-dependent feature importance curves show the varying importance of each predictor in AORSFM over time. (Figure 6A) The results indicate that apart from the increasing importance of “age” over time, the importance of other parameters remained stable. To further enhance the usability of the model, the study developed a web-based risk calculator. (https:// pgsxuliu.shinyapps.io/AORSFMforBC/) Additionally, the study developed a staging system based on AORSFM, utilizing the ST learner to categorize BC patients into three risk groups according to AORSFM’s risk scores. KM survival curves demonstrate statistically significant differences in OS among the high-risk, medium-risk, and low-risk groups across the two cohorts. (Figures 6B-C).
